  "evidence": "Original N/E/U shows a sustained, coherent offset beginning near index 649 (sharp jump in all axes: N from ~-5 to -13, E from ~32 to 31–33, U from ~18 to 23–26) and persisting through ~689, with smooth motion within the interval and no return to pre-offset levels before index 690. P1 (639–678) starts too early and ends before the clear plateau stabilizes; P2 (645–685) captures most but misses the full onset at 649 and the tail beyond 685; P3 (649–689) aligns best with observed onset (index 649 jump) and interior stability (consistent high E/N/U until ~689), and is supported by the visual_interval best candidate (first=639, second=679) being suboptimal due to nuisance steps at 649/666/690—649 is a real onset, not nuisance. No opposing return is observed within the reviewed window, but the platform is sustained and distinct from surrounding motion. Thus only P3 is genuine.",
